P1 (aarch64, gen 32): **the finaliser footprints without the VCPU-link words** (namespace `K8`), generated by
`proofs/scratch/a64/g32/gen8.py` (gen 31's `gen7.py` with one more substitution) from the Lean dump
`proofs/scratch/a64/g32/cone.out` (gen 31's `cone.out`: runs 0–2, the cones of `fin_endpoint.blk`, `fin_ntfn.blk`,
`fin_reply.blk` and `fin_sc.blk`). Not edited by hand.

QueueFoot7's `K7.KW` covers every TCB field from offset 224 except the debug links, so it includes a thread's
bound-VCPU word (offset 3664, `layout::tcb::VCPU`) and its `RUN_VCPU` word (offset 3672,
crates/fl4-core/src/arch/aarch64/layout.rs). The VCPU typing `VcTy` (QueueVcTy) reads both words of every thread,
so a `K7` footprint does not show that a finaliser keeps it. The copy here differs from its source only by:
* `192` → `224` (as QueueFoot7);
* `K.val ≠ 3584` → `(K.val ≠ 3584 ∧ K.val ≠ 3664 ∧ K.val ≠ 3672)` (in `KW`, `KWB`, `kw_field`, `kwB_field`,
  `foot_field`, `footB_field`: the only occurrences), so **`K8.KW` / `K8.KWB` exclude the words 3664 and 3672**;
* in `kw0_not_dbg`, the one place where the KW clause's `3584` conjunct is passed to a lemma outside the cone
  (QueueFoot's `notDbgW_field`), `h4` → `h4.1` (the first component of the new conjunct);
* every name declared in namespace `K8`; lemmas whose last component is `kw` / `kwB` renamed `kw8` / `kwB8` (the
  ones about non-footprint types at `Fl4ProofsA64.P1.<Type>.kw8`).

Every new side goal `K ≠ 3664 ∧ K ≠ 3672` closed by the original tactic: the endpoint, notification, reply and SC
finalisers write no thread's VCPU-link word (the TCB words they write are `STATE` 3328, the IPC / SC / timer /
yield / notification fields, all different offsets). Main results: `K8.fin_endpoint.blk`, `K8.fin_ntfn.blk`,
`K8.fin_reply.blk`, `K8.fin_sc.blk`. New definitions and theorems only; no existing statement changed; no named
premise.
